          "source_issue_or_choice": "The frozen algorithm defines k as the current maximal index and immediately assigns that existing index to a new formula, breaking distinct/fresh indexing and the later completeness proof's rising-index fairness argument. Its displayed right-existential inference is labelled LeftR(exists) even though the principal formula and copied instance are on the right.",
